    "summary": "High‑energy Carrier Dome show with smoking Far From Me/Playing→Crazy Fingers and epic Sugar Magnolia",
    "review": "The September 24, 1982 Carrier Dome gig is a textbook example of the funky Dead in full flight. The first set rolls out solid classics – Jack Straw into Friend Of The Devil, a seamless China>Rider, and a beautiful Bird Song that sets a relaxed yet anticipatory mood. Then the second set ignites: Far From Me launches directly into a soaring Playing In The Band → Crazy Fingers space jam that showcases Jerry’s lead work at its most inspired, while Brent’s electric piano adds lush color. The band rides the momentum through Throwing Stones, an otherworldly post‑drums Space, and a quirky Iko Iko > Truckin' > Goin’ Down The Road Feeling Bad > Black Peter > Around & Around cascade that feels like a musical roller‑coaster. The night caps with a funky, high‑octane Sugar Magnolia jam and a heartfelt Brokedown Palace encore. Across all sources the performance is consistently described as “high energy” and “smoking,” making this one of the standout shows of the 1982 tour.",
